1
00:00:00,090 --> 00:00:04,320
Resgrid Big Board brings department
information into configurable widgets.

2
00:00:04,670 --> 00:00:08,310
Here, the Personnel table
shows operational status beside

3
00:00:08,310 --> 00:00:10,119
staffing, with a clock below it.

4
00:00:10,500 --> 00:00:14,789
A duty supervisor can use this display
to review readiness during a handover.

5
00:00:15,279 --> 00:00:19,020
The same approach can support a
security control room, search-and-rescue

6
00:00:19,020 --> 00:00:23,350
coordination desk, community paramedicine
or mental health response team,

7
00:00:23,620 --> 00:00:28,680
wildland contractor, industrial response
team, or fire and E M S department.

8
00:00:29,159 --> 00:00:32,810
This walkthrough builds a readable
board using fictional training data.

9
00:00:33,010 --> 00:00:34,700
Start on the empty dashboard.

10
00:00:35,100 --> 00:00:38,099
The message directs you to the
plus button in the upper right.

11
00:00:38,429 --> 00:00:40,510
Select it to open Add Widget.

12
00:00:40,869 --> 00:00:44,680
The chooser includes Calls,
Units, Personnel and Time.

13
00:00:45,039 --> 00:00:48,859
Add those four widgets for this
exercise, choosing each from the menu.

14
00:00:49,259 --> 00:00:51,699
The chooser also offers
other widget types.

15
00:00:52,070 --> 00:00:56,140
Add information for a specific
audience and purpose; a coordination

16
00:00:56,140 --> 00:00:59,609
desk and a shared briefing display
may need different amounts of detail.

17
00:00:59,869 --> 00:01:03,040
Open the settings gear in
the header and select Calls.

18
00:01:03,470 --> 00:01:04,950
Scroll to Widget Size.

19
00:01:05,350 --> 00:01:10,550
In this recorded desktop example, Width
is ten grid units and Height is four.

20
00:01:10,970 --> 00:01:14,659
Adjust the width and height sliders to
give the incident table enough room,

21
00:01:15,020 --> 00:01:17,249
then use Save to return to the board.

22
00:01:17,729 --> 00:01:19,809
Choose sizes for your actual display.

23
00:01:20,180 --> 00:01:25,139
A wider widget gives long incident names
and addresses more horizontal space, while

24
00:01:25,139 --> 00:01:27,510
additional height makes more rows visible.

25
00:01:27,719 --> 00:01:32,359
In Calls settings, find Column Order
and the instruction to use the arrows.

26
00:01:32,799 --> 00:01:38,829
Move Priority upward until the first
three columns are I D, Priority and Name.

27
00:01:39,249 --> 00:01:42,539
Use the up arrow on the
Priority row, then Save.

28
00:01:42,909 --> 00:01:44,850
This changes where the column appears.

29
00:01:45,200 --> 00:01:49,509
It helps a supervisor read an incident
identifier and its priority together.

30
00:01:49,919 --> 00:01:53,479
We will check the table itself next,
because the returned display is the

31
00:01:53,479 --> 00:01:55,470
useful confirmation of this setting.

32
00:01:55,739 --> 00:01:59,670
The Calls table now begins
with I D, Priority and Name.

33
00:02:00,169 --> 00:02:05,089
The warehouse-alarm exercise shows Urgent,
while the community medical standby and

34
00:02:05,089 --> 00:02:07,520
vehicle-rescue exercise show Routine.

35
00:02:08,070 --> 00:02:12,600
Address, Timestamp and Dispatched
provide more context across each row.

36
00:02:13,059 --> 00:02:15,450
Read these values together
when comparing work.

37
00:02:15,860 --> 00:02:20,759
The Dispatched column lists dispatched
recipients; this screen does not by itself

38
00:02:20,759 --> 00:02:25,180
verify that every recipient accepted the
assignment or arrived at the incident.

39
00:02:25,530 --> 00:02:29,010
Use the relevant response and
operational views for those checks.

40
00:02:29,149 --> 00:02:31,879
Open the gear again and
select Units Widget.

41
00:02:32,350 --> 00:02:36,460
In the column-order controls,
move State immediately after Name.

42
00:02:36,960 --> 00:02:41,260
Keep Station, Type and Timestamp
after those columns for this example.

43
00:02:41,720 --> 00:02:45,279
The Widget Size controls below
give this table a width of ten

44
00:02:45,370 --> 00:02:47,269
and a height of three grid units.

45
00:02:47,689 --> 00:02:49,380
Save and inspect the result.

46
00:02:49,910 --> 00:02:54,199
Putting the resource name beside its state
makes it easier to scan which vehicle or

47
00:02:54,199 --> 00:02:56,259
team needs attention during a briefing.

48
00:02:56,509 --> 00:03:00,940
On the resulting Units table,
Engine fifty-one is Available, Squad

49
00:03:00,940 --> 00:03:05,169
three is Responding, and Reserve
Engine fifty-one is Out of Service.

50
00:03:05,660 --> 00:03:09,160
The community-response vehicle
demonstrates that the table can include

51
00:03:09,160 --> 00:03:11,330
resources beyond fire apparatus.

52
00:03:11,660 --> 00:03:15,309
A security patrol vehicle or
industrial response resource can

53
00:03:15,309 --> 00:03:17,410
be organized using the same fields.

54
00:03:17,799 --> 00:03:20,000
Read Updated as well as State.

55
00:03:20,420 --> 00:03:25,299
Several fictional exercise entries are
days old, so a displayed state alone is

56
00:03:25,299 --> 00:03:27,619
not evidence of a fresh readiness report.

57
00:03:27,760 --> 00:03:31,939
Select Personnel in the configuration
tabs and find Column Order.

58
00:03:32,450 --> 00:03:37,449
For this example, place Status immediately
after Name, followed by Group and

59
00:03:37,449 --> 00:03:40,089
Staffing, then Timestamp and Roles.

60
00:03:40,619 --> 00:03:44,350
Use the arrows on each row to
move the columns, then Save.

61
00:03:44,860 --> 00:03:48,780
This arrangement brings an individual
and their operational status together

62
00:03:49,069 --> 00:03:52,399
while keeping team assignment,
staffing and qualifications

63
00:03:52,399 --> 00:03:54,300
visible elsewhere in the same row.

64
00:03:54,829 --> 00:03:58,700
Choose a sequence that your supervisors
can read consistently during handover.

65
00:03:58,939 --> 00:04:02,770
The Personnel table shows Status
and Staffing as separate columns.

66
00:04:03,140 --> 00:04:06,900
In this exercise, Darren Ritter
has Standing By under Status

67
00:04:07,029 --> 00:04:08,569
and Delayed under Staffing.

68
00:04:09,020 --> 00:04:11,690
Blake Gallo has Standing
By and Unavailable.

69
00:04:12,090 --> 00:04:15,470
These are different pieces of
information, so read both before

70
00:04:15,470 --> 00:04:17,449
deciding that someone is ready for work.

71
00:04:17,859 --> 00:04:22,029
Roles and Group add organizational
context, and Updated provides

72
00:04:22,029 --> 00:04:23,750
the displayed age of the entry.

73
00:04:24,209 --> 00:04:28,689
The Time widget below supplies a visible
clock alongside the readiness information.

74
00:04:28,909 --> 00:04:31,919
Return to the dashboard and
select Edit in the header.

75
00:04:32,320 --> 00:04:35,309
The button changes to Done,
and widget headings show a

76
00:04:35,309 --> 00:04:37,260
grip and a red removal control.

77
00:04:37,709 --> 00:04:41,999
A temporary Notes widget has been added
beside Time for this layout exercise.

78
00:04:42,419 --> 00:04:44,819
The grip is the place to
begin moving the widget.

79
00:04:45,230 --> 00:04:48,529
Check the heading before using
a removal control, so you change

80
00:04:48,529 --> 00:04:52,089
the intended panel rather than
another widget on a crowded display.

81
00:04:52,310 --> 00:04:55,589
Drag the temporary Notes widget
by its heading grip to the right.

82
00:04:55,999 --> 00:04:59,359
The resulting view shows Notes
farther across the board, with

83
00:04:59,359 --> 00:05:00,910
Time remaining on the left.

84
00:05:01,290 --> 00:05:02,710
This is a layout change.

85
00:05:02,920 --> 00:05:05,479
It does not change the
department note itself.

86
00:05:05,840 --> 00:05:09,770
Use the same placement check when
arranging a shared display: confirm

87
00:05:09,770 --> 00:05:13,319
the final location of the panel
and make sure important information

88
00:05:13,350 --> 00:05:16,459
is still visible at the distance
from which people will read it.

89
00:05:16,560 --> 00:05:20,030
Select the red removal control
on the temporary Notes widget.

90
00:05:20,480 --> 00:05:23,840
That panel disappears, and the
board returns to four widgets:

91
00:05:24,179 --> 00:05:27,160
Calls, Units, Personnel and Time.

92
00:05:27,610 --> 00:05:31,230
The pictured lower part of the board
shows Personnel and Time remaining.

93
00:05:31,620 --> 00:05:33,549
Select Done to leave edit mode.

94
00:05:34,070 --> 00:05:37,820
Removing this display widget does not
delete the underlying department note.

95
00:05:38,250 --> 00:05:42,500
Keep only the panels needed for this
particular display, then check that

96
00:05:42,500 --> 00:05:44,500
its important tables remain readable.

97
00:05:44,719 --> 00:05:47,030
Reload Big Board to
check the saved result.

98
00:05:47,489 --> 00:05:51,109
Calls still begins with
I D, Priority and Name.

99
00:05:51,549 --> 00:05:55,440
Scroll down to confirm that Personnel
keeps its chosen sequence and

100
00:05:55,440 --> 00:05:56,999
that Time remains on the board.

101
00:05:57,520 --> 00:06:00,640
In this example, the larger
tables require scrolling.

102
00:06:01,039 --> 00:06:05,039
For a wall display, choose a smaller
set of panels that fits the screen

103
00:06:05,080 --> 00:06:07,160
and verify it on the actual monitor.

104
00:06:07,500 --> 00:06:11,330
For an interactive coordination
desk, decide which tables staff will

105
00:06:11,330 --> 00:06:13,180
scroll through during routine work.
